---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import '../styles/landing.css';
import Install from '../components/site/Install.astro';
import release from '../data/release.json';
const repo = 'https://github.com/ibrahemid/writ';
const sumsUrl = `${repo}/releases/download/${release.tag}/SHA256SUMS.txt`;
---
<Site title="Download Writ" description="Writ for macOS, Windows and Linux. Signed builds, package-manager one-liners, SHA256 checksums." path="/download/">
  <main class="page" id="top" style="padding-top:0">
    <Install standalone />
    <section class="band doc" style="padding-top:48px">
      <div class="doc-body">
        <h2 style="margin-top:0">Requirements</h2>
        <table>
          <tr><th>macOS</th><td>12 Monterey or later. One build for Apple silicon and Intel. Signed and notarized.</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Windows</th><td>10 or later, 64-bit. The .msi is not code-signed yet, so SmartScreen shows a warning on first run: More info, then Run anyway. The checksum below is how to verify it instead.</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Linux</th><td>x86_64. The AppImage runs anywhere with FUSE; the .deb targets Debian and Ubuntu. Arch has <code>writ-bin</code> on the AUR.</td></tr>
        </table>
        <h2>Verify a download</h2>
        <p>Every release ships a <a href={sumsUrl}>SHA256SUMS.txt</a>. On macOS or Linux:</p>
        <pre><code>shasum -a 256 Writ_{release.version}_universal.pkg</code></pre>
        <p>Compare the output with the line for that file. The current sums:</p>
        <table>
          <tr><th>.pkg</th><td><code>{release.platforms.mac.sha256_pkg}</code></td></tr>
          <tr><th>.dmg</th><td><code>{release.platforms.mac.sha256_dmg}</code></td></tr>
          <tr><th>.msi</th><td><code>{release.platforms.win.sha256_msi}</code></td></tr>
          <tr><th>.AppImage</th><td><code>{release.platforms.linux.sha256_appImage}</code></td></tr>
          <tr><th>.deb</th><td><code>{release.platforms.linux.sha256_deb}</code></td></tr>
        </table>
        <h2>Updates</h2>
        <p>Writ checks GitHub Releases on start and offers the new version; nothing installs without a click. The check verifies a signed manifest and can be turned off in Settings. Package-manager installs update through the package manager instead.</p>
        <h2>Uninstall</h2>
        <p>Delete the app. Your notes stay in <code>~/.writ</code> in your home folder until you delete that folder too.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Site>
